-- title:
--   Rational coefficient bound arrays for the row-9 inverse branches
-- statement:
--   These are explicit finite coefficient data for the degree-9 inverse cubic of a fifth power of $z^3-z-\beta$. The algebraic parameter used in the later proofs satisfies $\alpha^3=1001/2-462\alpha+84\alpha^2$. This bundle supplies twelve finite rational arrays: bounds for the coefficients of $P,Q,E,J$ for each of the three isolating real-root intervals. The arrays for $P,Q$ have 32 entries and those for $E,J$ have 62 entries.
--
--   They are the data for inequalities of the form
--   $$|c_j(\alpha)|\le B_j,\qquad |t|\le2.$$
--   The coefficient inequalities, their weighted sums and the resulting analytic contraction estimates are proved separately in Lean. These definitions contain only the explicit bound values.
-- source:
--   https://gist.github.com/Amal-David/adce933460b7501cb123f483f62775eb/f5a76eda649f3e995a8ec6b98387b23b64c6debb#file-fifth-md; H5_COMPLETE_CHAIN.md, Sections 1–4; lower/H5_LOWER_MIDDLE_COMPLETION.md and upper/H5_UPPER_BRIDGE.md in the archived research checkpoint. The finite Newton coefficient arrays are auxiliary exact certificates constructed for the accompanying Lean formalization, and are specified in full by this definition submission.

